{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix","id":846408,"title":"What If There Were More Types Of Strix?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-12T20:06:01-08:00","id":846408,"title":"What If There Were More Types Of Strix?","content":"I know one of their nicknames is Birds Of Dis, but what if they can take on the shape and demeanor of other animals? I can imagine some being more wolf-like, others more reptilian. The glowing eyes and shadow-smoke composition would probably remain, though. Any significant differences could be explained by sub-divisions inside Dis, or maybe Dis is a fusion of multiple Lower Depths. I remember a comment from somewhere on these forums, I think it was made by LostLight. It said that Longinus was visited by a very weird Strix of light and water, and that this visit influenced his decision to start the cult that would become the Lancea.<br /> <br /> Whatever shapes they take and whatever tricks they have, I believe they follow the same rules of Animalism: they can appear as predators and parasites, but never prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T20:25:56-08:00","id":846411,"title":"","content":"I like the Strix as birds, but I do like playing with the idea of different types besides just owls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T04:54:45-07:00","id":846523,"title":"","content":"I never liked the idea of the strix as all birds. Always rubbed me the wrong way. It feels very exclusive. Like, it was drawn from one mythology and made to be the whole thing. Personally, I don't even bother with familiar shapes, and just describe them as different kinds of living shadows - completely mutable without set form. Shadowy shapeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:08:01-07:00","id":846526,"title":"","content":"Oh, hell yeah. I can easily imagine the more powerful (ie bigger) ones taking the form of big black dogs, a la the Grim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T08:36:01-07:00","id":846581,"title":"","content":"Since i like the idea that strix are a type of personification of the beast i've maed 5 types of strix (one to reflect the beast of each clan)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:00:03-07:00","id":846588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846581#post846581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since i like the idea that strix are a type of personification of the beast i've maed 5 types of strix (one to reflect the beast of each clan)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you go into that a little more? You have my interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:58:11-07:00","id":846660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846523#post846523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked the idea of the strix as all birds. Always rubbed me the wrong way. It feels very exclusive. Like, it was drawn from one mythology and made to be the whole thing. Personally, I don't even bother with familiar shapes, and just describe them as different kinds of living shadows - completely mutable without set form. Shadowy shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure if being completely mutable is fitting for all of them. Mutability is the strong point of the Idigam. The strong point of the Strix, as I see it, is possession. I do agree they could incorporate ideas from other mythologies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846581#post846581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since i like the idea that strix are a type of personification of the beast i've maed 5 types of strix (one to reflect the beast of each clan)</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with Aiden. Could you please tell us more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:31:12-07:00","id":846677,"title":"","content":"Well i've simply taken each vampire archetype represented by each clan and taken it to a point where there is no humanity and from that i can interpret a personality and motivation. The 'mehket' strix, so to speak, would be occult, secretive and superstitious. its motivation could be that each vampire with a ring on his left hand must be destroyed. A 'nosferatu' strix could have for motivation that each vampires should be hated and alone. For me its simply a tools that helps me create a working personality. Tho i've never thought of making them something else than owl and i think its a great idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:49:00-07:00","id":846683,"title":"","content":"Strix being the reason for black cats being considered unlucky could be fun to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:59:16-07:00","id":846686,"title":"","content":"If you had to pick one animal for each strix-clan, what would they be? Mekhet is the owl that watches, Nosferatu is the rat that scurries hidden and hated, Gangrel is the feral wolf, Daeva is the big cat, that transfixes you with its stare and devours you, Ventrue is the hawk that flies above them all? <br /> <br /> Something similar to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:02:52-07:00","id":846689,"title":"","content":"Mekhet would probably be spider, Gangrel cat, Daeva snake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:37:56-07:00","id":846709,"title":"","content":"For nosferatu i could see either a cockroach or even a shadowy smoky swarm of cockroach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:49:11-07:00","id":846715,"title":"","content":"Traditionally they're associated with worms, as well. I enjoy linking them with frogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T14:12:39-07:00","id":846719,"title":"","content":"For the ventrue, i think i'd see yes the hawk but also the black dog","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:20:54-07:00","id":846740,"title":"","content":"I'd go with something regal for Ventrue, like a horse (the animal associated with the sin of Pride) or a lion (symbolically associated with royalty, &quot;king of the jungle&quot; and all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:41:32-07:00","id":846757,"title":"","content":"I figured owls for Ventrue, especially given the hate-on the standard owl strix seem to have had for them in first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:48:27-07:00","id":846760,"title":"","content":"Could a sufficiently powerful Strix possess an entire forest, extending its senses to fauna and flora? Not every cautionary tale about avoiding the woods at night has to be started by the fae, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:58:39-07:00","id":846767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846660#post846660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure if being completely mutable is fitting for all of them. Mutability is the strong point of the Idigam. The strong point of the Strix, as I see it, is possession. I do agree they could incorporate ideas from other mythologies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why should I care one whit about the Idigam in a Vampire game? And you're really taking what I'm saying a bit out of context. The Idigam turn into anything - spirits, physical, whatever. The strix are still shadows. Shadows are known for scary shapes out of the corner of your eye, not all animal shapes. And the latter is what I'm going for. The two, even with my suggestion, aren't comparable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-13-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T16:03:57-07:00","id":846769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846767#post846767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why should I care one whit about the Idigam in a Vampire game? And you're really taking what I'm saying a bit out of context. The Idigam turn into anything - spirits, physical, whatever. The strix are still shadows. Shadows are known for scary shapes out of the corner of your eye, not all animal shapes. And the latter is what I'm going for. The two, even with my suggestion, aren't comparable.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see what you mean. Sorry if I sounded demeaning or close-minded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T16:19:08-07:00","id":846779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846757#post846757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured owls for Ventrue, especially given the hate-on the standard owl strix seem to have had for them in first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say owls for Julii for sure. If they are also for Ventrue or Gangrel would be an ST call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T16:35:11-07:00","id":846789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846760#post846760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a sufficiently powerful Strix possess an entire forest, extending its senses to fauna and flora? Not every cautionary tale about avoiding the woods at night has to be started by the fae, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would take a weirdass dread power, but sure. <br /> <br /> As for the whole mutability thing, I think at least part of the reason that strix take avian forms is because they can fly. Even if one prefers being cat-shaped, it would probably subconsciously pop some wing shapes if it took to the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:19:21-07:00","id":846894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846789#post846789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would take a weirdass dread power, but sure.<br /> <br /> As for the whole mutability thing, I think at least part of the reason that strix take avian forms is because they can fly. Even if one prefers being cat-shaped, it would probably subconsciously pop some wing shapes if it took to the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well i dont think we have to figure a scientific reasoning for how they can fly with or without wings, tho i would say like smoke they are lighter than air. <br /> Also i think i would like a bat form, i am a traditionalist at heart. i think the bat could fit with the concept of any clan really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T03:29:38-07:00","id":846993,"title":"","content":"Oh, they don't <i>need</i> wings to fly. I just think it would look a bit weird if they kept a non-winged shape when they did. It's an aesthetic thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T03:53:37-07:00","id":847001,"title":"","content":"I've been in a Vampire game in which the strix just looked like shadows of whatever they wanted to look like shadows of. Like the shadow-creatures from disney's princess and the frog (and I know it's an awful movie).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T04:00:07-07:00","id":847003,"title":"","content":"Strix are owls because reasons <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(genus\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(genus</a>) in general and because reasons <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(mythology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(mythology</a>) more specific. There is really no need to water down the realworld mythology for the strix by other creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T04:43:53-07:00","id":847012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=847003#post847003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strix are owls because reasons <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(genus\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(genus</a>) in general and because reasons <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(mythology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(mythology</a>) more specific. There is really no need to water down the realworld mythology for the strix by other creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although i agree that the mythology of the strix is a treasure trove of story idea. the fact of the matter is that it has a decidedly greek origin. <br /> the point here, as i understand it, is adapting the core concept of what the strix means in the game to use other mythology.<br /> for exemple one could use the mythology of the camazotz of south america instead of the strix and have the shadow thing appear as bats instead of owls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:12:55-07:00","id":847018,"title":"","content":"Owls are popular shapes, but strix are individuals. They're not all going to conform to the stereotypes. Why are they a bat? They like bats. What of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T03:58:28-07:00","id":848070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846408-what-if-there-were-more-types-of-strix?p=846769#post846769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see what you mean. Sorry if I sounded demeaning or close-minded.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, you didn't. I just wanted to make a point that I don't care about what other games do when talking about a specific game. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T22:57:22-07:00","id":852255,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of having breeds of Strix specifically linked to each clan, since it would tend to lend more credence to the idea that the Strix are actually the progenitors of every clan. I'm fine with the idea that the Strix may have been involved in the creation of <i>some</i> of the clans; the Ventrue come to mind, and possibly the Gangrel by extension, while some of the Daeva mythology from their clanbook points to the Strix having a hand in their origin as well. But I'd also like for at least some of the clans to have entirely different origins, possibly even beginning as something like the Jiang-Shi presented in the core book: unrelated monsters who somehow became more similar to the Kindred through long association with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:48:03-07:00","id":852430,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm intrigued by that snippet in the Mekhet clanbook about a primordial shadow ambush predator from when Homo sapiens sapiens wasn't quite a thing yet.<br /> I like the following ideas regarding the origin of the Mekhet:<br /> <br /> 1) that is <i>ultimately </i>lies with some extremely ancient obtenebration-ish creatures with some things in common with the Strix but which were emphatically not Strix;<br /> 2) that there were multiple &quot;steps&quot; between those things and the Egyptian Hollow Ones (which were lost to (pre-)history), while other Clans may have been created by the Owls in a more direct way;<br /> 3) that the Khaibit basically managed to harness what is basically an atavism to counter the Strix.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T10:32:10-07:00","id":852474,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of all things Glass Armonium, myself. My personal theory is that the tentacled cave-creature that Francis experienced when she used the Armonium created the first Mekhet by using its &quot;blades&quot; to carve away and devour a human's shadow and part of their soul, before slipping into the metaphysical hollow place it had created. The creature and its spawn still dwell within the Mekhet, though in the case of non-Hollow they lie mostly dormant, or else have grown so close to the former human's own soul that they are largely indistinguishable from it.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Hollow, however, these spiritual parasites have learned to imitate its prey in order to facilitate its feeding. In fact, they may have learned a little <i>too</i> well, such that they now believe themselves to <i>be</i> their host, or at least a genuine part of their host's soul. This might mean that a Hollow Mekhet's erstwhile reflection/ghost is one of these primordial creatures, but that begs the question of why the reflection can go forth by day, when their ancient shadow-creature progenitor was confined to the darkness.<br /> <br /> A more disturbing possibility is this: the reflection really <i>is</i> the Mekhet's ghost, a tattered remnant of a partially devoured soul, while the being that now walks around in her skin and fears the light is an impostor, a predatory mimic so skilled that it has even fooled itself into believing that it was once human. That might help explain why the reflection seems to resent Mekhet so much: the vampire is a usurper who stole the reflection's life and forced her into a hellish existence as a hungry ghost.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> As for the Nosferatu, I'm a big fan of the idea that they're somehow linked with otherworldly creatures of a vaguely Lovecraftian character. I think it fits with the Nightmare discipline, since it causes maddening and increasingly elaborate hallucinations rather than simple fear. Maybe what the Nosferatu (and others who learn to make their blood resonate with the power of Nightmare) are unknowingly doing is granting glimpses of some kind of chthonic Otherworld, a realm of mind-shattering vistas and senseless torments from whence the progenitors of the Nosferatu first emerged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 03-24-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:28:59-07:00","id":853019,"title":"","content":"I think the fluff in some of the books has implied here and there that what has been called strix in contemporary nights <b>might</b> be the same creatures that created and tormented the Julii in ages past, but not exactly so and that a number of cases might involve beings of quite different origins or natures being conflated with them due to passing resemblance based on unreliable sources and such.<br /> <br /> <b>Kindred </b>have been calling them strix, doesn't mean all - or any - of them are indeed the Birds of Dis of old. It's one of the stealth answers behind the discrepancies in description (owls of smoke x owls/ravens/crows/vultures of shadows/dust/smoke/darkness) and capacities shown by them in Requiem for Rome/Fall of the Camarilla and the beings described in Night Horrors, Danse Macabre and Blood &amp; Smoke.<br /> <br /> Is a delicate winged silhouette seen in a fevered night an angel, Nike goddess of victory, a siren or one of the lilitu? Who knows, depends on context and even the viewer may get it wrong, what to say of later chroniclers/copyists. As the old saying goes, not all that shines is gold. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}